  "title": "Speech got more ways in and out",
  "summary": "More ways to build with audio, models, and agents came with clearer discovery, Quest progress, and Pollen costs.\n\nCommunity contributors added OpenAI-compatible transcription models, followed by GPT batch and live transcription. On the output side, `grok-tts` and `fish-audio-s2.1-pro` joined the existing speech endpoints. Unsupported subtitle formats now return a clear error instead of an empty response.\n\nAuthenticated accounts can test an upstream endpoint before registering a private model; requests to publish public models or agents have a clearer path. Owners can declare text-model capabilities, while listings distinguish community proxies and agents more consistently. Publishing guides now cover the dashboard, CLI, and API.\n\nModel cards became easier to compare across desktop and mobile, with clearer pricing, capabilities, access labels, and sorting. Model listings and the SDK now expose video duration options. The app catalog gained search across names, descriptions, and GitHub fields, shareable search and filter URLs, and nine community apps.\n\nManaged-agent responses now show tool names, arguments, and results or failures in both streaming and non-streaming output. Agents can use every tool advertised by an enabled Pollinations MCP server. Cost estimates, balance checks, and price sorting now account for the model steps and tool calls inside an agent run—not just its wrapper.",
